{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>To bathe at the river.</b> In the king's chamber, which adjoined the river and overlooked it. For indeed the honor of a king's daughter is indoors; she surely did not go out to the river." "<b>And her maidens walking.</b> Therefore she did not send one of them, for they were not then there with her." "<b>And she sent her maidservant.</b> The maidservant attending her then for bathing. And all this was by divine will, so that she would not send one of the important maidens and rely on her — in which case she might have chosen to throw him into the river."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:58.852968837Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}